        "transcript": [
          {
            "role": "user",
            "text": "I need the wall ready for finishing quickly. How does block installation compare with cast-in-situ curing?",
            "turn": 1,
            "at": "2026-08-22T14:33:19.524Z"
          },
          {
            "role": "assistant",
            "text": "When you are prioritizing speed, pre-cast hemp-lime blocks generally get your walls ready for finishing much faster than cast-in-situ. \n\nPre-cast blocks arrive already cured, so after laying them with lime mortar, you only need to wait about 2 to 3 days for the mortar to set before moving on to your plaster or finishing sequence. On the other hand, cast-in-situ requires building formwork, tamping the hemp-lime wet mix by hand or pneumatically, and waiting for a natural curing window of about 3 to 6 weeks depending on weather conditions before final plastering can safely begin.\n\nWould you like to calculate the total wall volume for your project so we can estimate how many blocks or materials you might need?",
            "turn": 1,
            "at": "2026-08-22T14:33:22.572Z"
          }
        ],
